proof='''# Independent scoped reconstruction and near-optimum rigidity

Uniform finite Boolean signs; entropy bits. Let a(f) be the minimum of I over invertible affine inputs and output characters, delta=Pr[f=-1], P=(-1)^p with GF2 degree p<=d, q=2^(1-d), gamma=q-4delta>=0, and r the affine dimension of Fourier support(P). For K>=0 put Daff=H-Ka.

1. Let Z be the directions along which P(x+v)/P(x) is constant. Fourier translation shows Z annihilates every difference between two support labels. Thus codim Z=r. After translating the support by a character it lies in a linear r-space U. Multiplication by P is an orthogonal convolution on each U-coset. Each coset squared mass is conserved. The chain rule for entropy, including zero-mass cosets, bounds its conditional entropy increase by r. Hence H(fP)-H(f)<=r. No support labels are thrown away.

2. A nonzero multilinear GF2 polynomial of degree b has relative weight at least 2^-b: split on a variable with nonzero derivative and induct, since at least one of the two fibres is one wherever that derivative is one. Apply also to its complement. A nonconstant derivative of p has degree<=d-1, so its centered disagreement is at least q. Every directional disagreement of f is at most 2delta, hence already centered (delta<=q/4<=1/4). Centering is distance to the two constant events; the XOR triangle inequality gives m_fP(v)>=m_P(v)-Inf_v(f). Off Z, m_fP(v)-m_f(v)>=q-2Inf_v(f)>=gamma. On Z these centered costs agree exactly.

3. For any independent input-direction basis, arbitrary output characters can prescribe its n derivative signs independently. Thus a(f) is precisely the minimum basis sum of centered directional costs. An optimizing basis for fP has at least r vectors outside Z. Its sum of f costs is at least a(f), and gamma>=0 permits replacing the active count by r. Therefore a(fP)>=a(f)+r gamma and Daff(fP)<=Daff(f)-r*(K gamma-1). This independently reconstructs A055 PROOF Sections1--2 and the elementary joint-orbit conclusion at the start of Section3, without repair. Affine substitution preserves degree, so arbitrary alternating phase/affine operations reduce to one phase and one affine map. This review does NOT adopt A055's arbitrary-core embedding, all-block estimates, NAND32 recursion or giant explicit certificate; those have separate dependencies.

4. NEW SCOPED COROLLARY. Set m=K gamma-1>0. For any joint phase/affine competitor g with H(g)-K I(g)>=Daff(f)-epsilon, epsilon>=0, its reduced phase has r<=epsilon/m, since its actual influence is at least its optimized influence. In particular epsilon<m forces r=0, and a Boolean phase with singleton Fourier support is exactly a signed character. This is true for ANY f under the rarity bound when comparing with Daff(f); to call f the actual root optimizer require I(f)=a(f). Constants and r=0 require no division by an influence. At epsilon=m the strict conclusion cannot be inferred. This corollary does not assert that rare sources have low H/I.

5. WHY CRITICALITY STILL MATTERS. On a genuine least-essential-dimensional positive K-witness every complete smaller Boolean child obeys H(child)<=K I(child). All of its affine/character transforms are also smaller Boolean functions, hence H(child)<=K a(child), and the SAME original full-terminal reserve S_A*=average[Ka(child)-H(child)] is nonnegative. This quantifies over complete children, not spectral components, and grants no inherited phase stationarity. A merely orbit-extremal rare embedding can have S_A*<0, however small its absolute magnitude. Neither the rank theorem nor near-optimum rigidity changes that sign. Component pruning cannot substitute: projected components need not be Boolean descendants and the mixed signed rows and their interference remain in the original bill. Root phase normalization is initial only; old debits and the original comparison rate persist.

6. FIRST UNSUPPORTED UNIVERSAL LINE. For sufficiently high absolute K, a genuine least-dimensional positive witness, jointly cubic/affine optimal initially, must possess an ORIGINAL proper pair whose complete mixed entropy bill, phase price Pi, and all old debits are paid from its SAME nonnegative complete-child reserve and unused independent quotient-rank release. Neither this review nor the rigidity corollary proves that selection statement. A054's paid rematched pair cannot omit Pi. Full FEI OPEN; universal constant improvement zero.
'''
put('RIGIDITY_REVIEW.md',proof)
statement='For finite uniform Boolean signs f and degree<=d phase P, let delta=Pr[f=-1], gamma=2^(1-d)-4delta>=0, a be full affine/character minimum influence, r the affine spectral rank of P, and m=K*gamma-1>0. Any joint degree<=d-phase/affine competitor g with H(g)-K I(g)>=H(f)-K a(f)-epsilon has r<=epsilon/m in its one-phase normal form. Thus epsilon<m forces that reduced phase to be a signed character. Actual root maximality additionally requires I(f)=a(f). This is a scoped rigidity corollary, not a child-funding theorem or FEI bound.'
